WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:02.409
- Go. - Hi, I'm Matt. This is Tom.

00:00:02.409 --> 00:00:04.569
And we're playing Chess Clock Jenga.

00:00:04.569 --> 00:00:06.640
Chess Clock Jenga is a massive improvement
on --

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.580
how did you do that that fast?!

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:11.750
Chess Clock Jenga is a massive improvement
on regular Jenga.

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:12.790
You lose if... aah!

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:16.199
...if your timer runs out on your clock on
the chess clock.

00:00:16.199 --> 00:00:18.180
Or if you knock the tower over.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.900
Now, chess clocks work -- for those who don't
know --

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:21.060
by having two separate clocks

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:25.220
that only count down on your own turn.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:28.890
So currently... we're pretty much exactly
tied.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:30.380
'Cos I had a couple of difficult moves,

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:31.449
Matt had a couple of difficult moves,.

00:00:31.449 --> 00:00:34.220
but right now his clock is counting down -- 40
seconds --

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:38.140
and mine isn't. So I've got a little bit of
breathing space,

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:40.280
a little bit of time!

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:44.510
But... that doesn't mean I can't still lose
if I do something like that.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:50.600
And the trouble is, Matt is very good at finding
that block

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.129
that is just not 'in there' with the rest
of the tower.

00:00:53.129 --> 00:00:55.850
And having said that, Matt, you're still ten
seconds behind me.

00:00:55.850 --> 00:01:00.250
Oh... oh, of course you got that one. Right,
wonderful.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.370
Can I take the... yes! Yes, I can take that
one.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:06.580
So you can't take from the top two levels,
same with regular Jenga,

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:08.300
but -- there we go...

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:11.680
But other than that, any block is fine.

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:14.280
Matt, you are still ten seconds... uh-oh.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:17.860
God, I'm loads behind. Tom, you've got 25
seconds on...

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:21.130
I'm fine(!) 17 for you. It's absolutely fine.

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:23.530
13 seconds, Matt.

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:26.250
So all Tom needs to do is not make the tower
fall over

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.320
and my timer will run out quickly.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:30.560
Oh, assuming I can find a block to move...

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:32.090
Aah! Aaaah!

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:34.380
15 seconds, Tom.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:38.800
Okay. No, I'm fine. I'm fine, I'm fine, I'm
fine...

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.090
12 seconds, Matt.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:46.610
10 seconds, Tom.

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:49.490
Aah! No! It's good, it's good, it's good,
I'm fine...

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:51.011
Five... four...

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:54.080
Five! Four! Three! Two!

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:01.140
Ah, come on!

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:03.770
And that is Chess Clock Jenga.

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:08.649
So much better than the original.

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:12.040
